# 🚨 Ultrasonic Proximity Security System

A real-time embedded system built using ESP32 that detects proximity and triggers alerts using multiple integrated subsystems including sensors, communication interfaces, and user feedback systems.

---

## 🧠 System Overview

This system continuously monitors distance using an ultrasonic sensor and reacts dynamically by updating visual indicators, triggering alerts, and communicating system status through multiple interfaces.

---

## ⚙️ Key Features

- 📏 Ultrasonic distance sensing with signal filtering
- 📊 LED bar graph for real-time proximity visualization
- 📟 LCD display for live system feedback
- 📡 BLE communication for remote control (ARM, DISARM, STATUS, etc.)
- 🌐 WiFi web dashboard for real-time monitoring
- 🔔 Buzzer alert system with configurable modes
- 🧠 State-based logic (armed/disarmed system with trigger thresholds)

---

## 🔄 System Flow

1. Ultrasonic sensor measures distance  
2. ESP32 processes and filters data  
3. LED bar graph updates based on proximity  
4. System evaluates trigger conditions  
5. Alerts are activated if thresholds are exceeded  
6. Status is communicated via BLE, LCD, and web interface  

---

